# RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES — seven local fixes in chapters 25, 29 and 30

The movement is structurally sound and may close after the seven exact fixes below: three protected-unit restorations, three joins required by Pike's restored unit, and one Ring-sheet continuity repair. No scene move, calendar repair, canon redesign or withheld-truth repair is required. The two substantive defects are (a) Pike's source unit says he speaks unasked to the book, while the draft asks him directly and then repeats part of the protected content (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-08.md:171`; `manuscript/chapter-25.md:37-47`), and (b) the draft leaves Ring sheet eleven half rubbed although the packet requires a sheet to each of eleven uprights and the locked ending carries Ring 11 (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:99,123,163`; `EVENT-LIST.md:111`; `BOOK_MAP.md:35`).

## 1. Continuity with the closed text

### Findings

1. **Pike protected-unit join — FIX.** The full source sentence says Pike addresses the book and is “asked by nobody,” but Cael asks him about Teague immediately before the marker (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-08.md:171`; `manuscript/chapter-25.md:37-43`). The next draft paragraph also composes “read it twice” and “put it back under a stone,” both already present in the full protected unit (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-08.md:171`; `manuscript/chapter-25.md:47`). Fixes 1–4 put the ledger physically beside Pike, leave Cael's question unasked, restore the protected line exactly, and remove the duplicated protected facts.
2. **Ring rubbings — FIX.** The site has eleven uprights and the packet requires “a sheet to a stone: eleven,” while the surviving prose stops the eleventh halfway (`EVENT-LIST.md:110-114`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:19,99,123,163`). The locked ending requires Ring 11 among the 52 sheets (`BOOK_MAP.md:35`). Fix 7 completes the eleventh sheet without changing the den discovery or its timing (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:155-169`).

No other contradiction with closed Movement 3 survives.

### Entry state and carried continuity

- **People and bodies agree.** Closed day 84 has Cael's three left-low ribs broken on day 78, taped on day 81 until day 99, and his calf cloth-bound but not mended; Movement 4 opens with exactly those states (`STATE_LEDGER.md:395`; `manuscript/chapter-23.md:5`). Closed Lira has a day-80-mended tibia barred from running for a month, an unmended taped ankle and no right boot; the draft preserves the new shin, unmended ankle, packed replacement boot and walking-only behavior (`STATE_LEDGER.md:397`; `manuscript/chapter-23.md:5,69-105,125,189`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:147-151`). Closed Brom's wrist restriction runs to the middle of day 87; he keeps it to the rod's shadow before lifting and later carries without a Path response (`STATE_LEDGER.md:399`; `manuscript/chapter-23.md:131-161,207-211`). Closed Karis is empty and under a one-week no-spark order from day 80; she sleeps through the road, then sets her first point on day 93 and reports three parts full on day 96 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:401`; `manuscript/chapter-23.md:5,127,227`; `manuscript/chapter-26.md:247-253`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:23-43`). Seln remains unmarked (`STATE_LEDGER.md:403`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:155-159`).
- **Oryn's prior plan changes on the page at the required place.** Her closed window allocates the extra span as four table days plus one added deep-reading day (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:223-231`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:431`). At Thornwater's gate she first states the table-through-day-100 plan, then substitutes two days out, two back and the site's time, with the same six other gates waiting the same days; she adds Cael as a stop herself (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:195-215`).
- **Money and debts close.** The prior balance is 116 in hand and six owed to the smith (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-331`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:409`). The replacement boots cost two, producing 114 (`manuscript/chapter-23.md:69-105,257`); the smith receives six, producing 108 (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:227-245`). The ferryman refuses silver and records a sixty-yard, four-strand rope owed in kind with no price, so the purse does not move (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:3-21`).
- **The boxes and carried objects agree.** All three recovered boxes ride the Oxhollow grain cart (`STATE_LEDGER.md:409`; `manuscript/chapter-23.md:7,21-27,257`). At Thornwater, two stay in the loft; the sealed five-thumb reserve remains in the third; the chips, lamp, calfskin, printed sheet and clean paper go in the middle box (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:3-19`). The hedging bill survives and goes inside (`STATE_LEDGER.md:399`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:7`). Seln's case enters shut on its strap and remains so at the close (`STATE_LEDGER.md:403`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:177`), and Hesk's satchel carries the log and both new letters forward (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:35-39`; `manuscript/chapter-27.md:53-101`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:219-231`). The lost cart, original blankets, kettle, canvas, flour and ferryman's rope are never resurrected; Thornwater lends a new roll of six blankets (`STATE_LEDGER.md:358`; `manuscript/chapter-23.md:43,253`; `manuscript/chapter-27.md:21-29`).
- **Standings agree.** The traverse becomes line seven, the five rise to tenth, and Teague is nine up (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:73-105`; `manuscript/chapter-25.md:3-19`). The two HOLD slips still carry the five names and remain unresolved (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:37-57`; `manuscript/chapter-25.md:59-63,245-253`).
- **Knowledge agrees.** Oryn enters knowing only that surface readings cannot find Cael and knowing nothing of fragments (`STATE_LEDGER.md:405,413`); by the close she has learned only the common line effect and still knows nothing about the fragments (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:181-233,239-299`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:179,187`). Teague's window stays within what he can know from the plank, the posting and his three (`STATE_LEDGER.md:407`; `manuscript/chapter-25.md:53-105`). Ephram's “Bracken” is male, and Vell's “The session still stands” remains unexplained (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:59-83`; `manuscript/chapter-27.md:55-97`).
- **Fragment accounting agrees.** Movement 3 closes at nine confirmed fragments, Shadow sealed and deployment since the Line one (`STATE_LEDGER.md:395`). The private Iron/Wind tests are unwitnessed, the floor read is recorded only as *No seam*, Shadow is refused, and the day-96 log omits rather than changes the deployment count (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:239-299`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:63-77,219-235`). Deployment since the Line therefore remains **one** (`BOOK_MAP.md:180,186-188`).

## 2. The movement plan

### Beats, order and withholding

All packet beats occur in order: the day-84-to-90 cart road and physical problem (`manuscript/chapter-23.md:13-27,47-67,165-219`); day-90 HOLD slips, traverse, posting, Pike, maps, smith and Lira (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:35-57,61-101,117-223,227-275`); wall, Teague window, one council, Part-1 log and day-91 witnessing (`manuscript/chapter-25.md:3-49,53-105,109-217,221-253`); mail, letters, paired maps and day-93 Thornwater (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:3-39,43-149,155-261`); the day-94/95 road and line (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:3-39,43-153,157-255`); the night test, perimeter and stake (`manuscript/chapter-28.md:3-61,65-219`); the five live-Arbiter trials and Cael's two private tests (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:3-235,239-299`); and six over, the floor, absent instruments, den and far-lip log (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:3-129,131-239`). The only packet-beat defect is the half eleventh rubbing ruled above (`EVENT-LIST.md:111`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:163`).

Withholding is intact. *Quieting* never occurs; “Compact” is never spoken; the iron carries the registry's stamp; no stillhound is seen; Oryn reads nobody inside; Seln's map memory is not spent; and only Karis says “made” of the place (`manuscript/chapter-28.md:113-137,169-181,211-217`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:211-227`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:103-117,155-197`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:51-57`). Cael's two tests are private, Shadow is untouched, and the five live Arbiters fail at the same step while his own Arbiter is described outside protected text only as dark since Kindling (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:185-229,255`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:239-299`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:63-77,219-235`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:154-157`).

The reported source-distance probe is the required **4% skeleton / 21% close** (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:10,106`).

