editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:129:**Physical challenge or learning encounter per movement:** M1 the wash recovery, the hold drilled, the Thornwater stretch walked at dusk · M2 the ford (developed fight), the well, Lira's first runs on a stiff ankle · M3 the fan haul, the bench, the stampede (terrain fight), the lip · M4 the perimeter walk and the six trials inside the line (a learning encounter for every one of the six) · M5 the Ring (central set piece), the deep reading · M6 **the deliberate quieter movement:** the bowman's one-armed shooting lessons, Cael relearning the Wind economy in Thornwater's yard under the listening, and the strata demonstration · M7 the run to the stair, the stalemate, the ascent and the rim · M8 the wyrm trials and the Hall, then the walk home into first snow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:144:| **Teague** | 8,200 (2.7%) | M1: 1,500 (day 49, the door: counting his three, then the job, then the five) · M3: 1,400 (Oxhollow's ford at dusk: the four sentences as a price) · M4: 1,200 (day 89: reading the Fallow slip twice, putting it back, telling Pike) · M7: 2,400 (days 113–115: not back from the Stair, the walk south to look, the rim's ground read, the crossbows, holding the rim at dawn) · M8: 1,700 (days 117–120: following the trail with the healer, sitting down beside the boy, "a new column") | What a captain reads off ground, faces and paper; the board; his own unreported Bronze and why ("I'd sooner be worth what I did than what they wrote"); that the Stair slip was wrong, by instinct; what he saw on the rim (a declaration *outside* the line) | The mechanism; anything working *inside* a line; any crew member's name; any Compact link beyond "a bad contract"; any envy or villainy — he is honest, priced, and the mirror of a found family without a Cael in it |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:145:| **Seln** | 7,600 (2.5%) | M1: 1,800 (days 10–40: walking every road out of Lowmarch, and later Thornwater, alone; the report nobody asks for) · M5: 2,000 (day 97, at the stone, then the stake: the maps with holes unlocking; ends as he asks for the carter's map) · M7: 2,200 (night of day 112: the second slip held against the first in his head; twelve years carrying the case; wanting a face) [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B6, C2] · M8: 1,600 (days 124–128: the ledger in his coat on the road home; giving it to Karis) | His fifteen years; the maps he carried and their blanks; the registry's form-prose; the case's known contents (the machine's maintenance records, read in B6); his read of the trap; his anger | Where the Quieting file is or what it says ("I carried the maps. I never saw the file."); any face or name on the rim; the case opened; the index decoded; the stroke-and-bar decoded; any sentence of affection said aloud |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:161:| Brom | Worth without a number | Holds the road on a stone he found at noon; drops Iron Skin in one contact; asks Pike what the board pays a man with no Path and writes the answer down; goes back for two boxes; "Cart's gone"; holds the lip Pathless; quotes Rooke (the first person he has ever quoted); carries the case and refuses help three times; stops to give Karis a shoulder; "Twice" | 16 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:164:| Oryn | The route: the only thing she owns | Comes up a lip because a carter said a crew was late; refuses the ankle on arithmetic; tests the line alone eight times; sets the condition and the terms; leaves her mule with the crew; sends word up the route and comes south as a stop; refuses the lean-to request, grants the road; goes into the water; turns north at the fork | 20 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:165:| Teague | To stay worth what he did, with his people counted first | Reads the Fallow slip twice and puts it back; puts the Stair slip back; "we'll come look" — and comes; holds the rim unasked; brings his healer three days along a bearing; asks "What are you" plainly; gives the five the cold-term fence; sets an after-thaw term [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] | 12 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:196:**Others' progression:** Lira learns to be fast with nothing at the end (M2), and learns to shoot braced one-armed (M6 → M8). Brom learns Iron Skin is a shout out here, and what he is without it ("a big man with good footwork and a lip of fused stone"). Karis learns to keep one point; the lattice line across a mountain; the wall along a line from her knees. Seln learns that his Path "was never most of what I do." Oryn: what her hands can and cannot do at a line, tested eight times alone. Teague: a column he does not have.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:211:| M3 | The lip, thirty-one paces, three ribs, a new leg | 1,200 | Hazard |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:242:**Documents, slips and notices**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:246:- The Fallow slip (Ch8, Ch12): *Recovery. Surveyor's instruments abandoned at a site on the Fallow road. East of Thornwater; the second day; where the road leaves its line at the rise and comes back to it. One hundred marks (one hundred).* Seal: a hook and a bar, in dark wax.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:248:- The Stair slip (Ch17): *Recovery. Surveyor's instruments abandoned at a site on the Stair road. South of Lowmarch; the first day; where the road drops off the ridge and the ground opens. Three hundred marks (three hundred).*

codex
The fence is not the planned job: the source and downstream packets identify it as the axe-head hold’s long forty-mark fence, still unfinished when the Stair pulls Teague away. The repair’s upper-inn paddock (three days, five marks) would erase that continuity. I’ve also confirmed the time-overrun change now conflicts with Movement 5’s inherited “quarter-hour” pressure; I’m checking the exact baseline wording and all affected joins before drafting fixes.
