     6	
     7	The healer was not at her table. She was in the long house, eating, and when she had eaten she climbed the gate-house ladder and slept.
     8	
     9	"There's people waiting," said Lira, to the woman who kept the gate. "There's a boy on that bench with his arm in a scarf."
