All KEEP except two settled by line fix. In particular: the manuscript's distances govern (the
western line stone 220 yards from the floor's middle; the six on the eastern lip) and Movement 5
inherits them — "a hundred and fifty yards inside" is dropped from the plan; no cord length or
stride length is to be added; the trial order and Brom's box; your reason for Cael's silence; the
two extra blanks marked *guess*; Oxhollow's grain cart; the rope owed in kind; the money; the two
HOLD slips left open; the day-96 log without its deployment line. Amended: the three markers, and
the eleventh Ring sheet (finished, not half rubbed — the plan needs a sheet to each of eleven
uprights).

## Already applied by the coordinator — DO NOT UNDO (smooth the joins only)
1. **ch25, Pike on Teague — the protected unit, whole:**
   `"Teague's nine up," Pike said, to the book, asked by nobody. Then, still to the book, at the
   same size, as if it were the next line and not a different thing: "He read that slip yesterday.
   Read it twice, same as the boy did. Put it back under the stone and took the fence. I'd have
