- **A, one beat.** The brief asked for one strap-and-case beat and an amended inventory. I gave the beat at the ford and a single sentence at the east gate as well, since the review named both places as leaving it unaccounted for.
- **B2, the re-entry.** I followed the suggested route, with one difference: Karis is already on the floor when Lira sees the bands (chapter 30's first scene ends with the tenth cord in her hand at the middle), so it is the other five who are drawn over the rim.
- **E, the sun.** While re-reading chapter 30 I found that "two hands above the hills" and "a quarter of an hour" could not both bring the sun to the ridge. The quarter of an hour that Cael gives now "runs to three" (the torn tenth sheet), which he names at ch30:219. This is a change of fact inside the limits of the plan.
