editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md-49-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:50:Day 115, at the stone in full sun. The kit is on Brom's good shoulder and his bad one is mended once. Lira's arm is closed again with the sling higher. The ledger is in Seln's coat; twenty-nine sheets and forty-one kinds. A brass edge lies on a map. A dead man's last word was *bearing*. "We're going to go look."
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-22-The found family's together-fight, terrain-first and Pathless. The still place told, with the reader's hand on the healer's wrist. The book's moral stake paid by *not* reading a man. Four sites on a line. First snow, a ledger that admits it is too small, and a sixth chair filled by post. Turns and promises:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-23-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-24-- **The bearing walk (116–118), on the page:** a road, then a track, then a carter's memory. Karis does not once say *if*. The country going into the last mild days. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and eighty-five yards. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:26:- **The trials (≈2,500), from the hall's outer coping inside the perimeter (EXC-B7-005):** the causeway crossing, with her hands checked at the stride both ways; the rule walking with them; the bulge once in a quarter-hour; a stone at eleven; Lira's skipping stone answered only where it stops, at fourteen; **Seln's rule in his own hand on Karis's page** ("It's blind… it strikes what *stays*."); **Cael's Anchor point** held for sixty counts ("It reads that as the heaviest thing…" / "…the thing that *stays*."). The council at the stone (protected Lira lines). Camp at the line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:27:- **Day 119, the Hall (≈5,000–6,000):** Brom *stops* to put Karis up the wall and the floor opens under him; he puts her up before he goes sideways. "Get *off* the floor." **The coping** as cover and trap. Karis copying the wall she kneels on, funny for exactly one exchange. **Brom's shoulder opens**; he slips on the wrong wall. **Oryn into the water, skipping**, the healer reaching a falling patient (not heroic, only nearest). **The second pass turns** toward where she is going. **Cael in, declaring:** Compression takes the strike into a standing frame at the broken edge; **Anchor laid on the floor** at the broken centre. "A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest." It surfaces whole for the first time in anyone's memory. "Brom. Wall. Your weight. Now." **Four bolts into the pale**: Lira twice, braced one-armed against the coping and a knee, with Seln spanning between (the bowman's lessons pay); Seln twice. The point released; the jaws close on water; it lets go and goes down, alive. "Walls… Twelve sheets." It is left there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-28-- **Costs at the track's end:** Oryn's hour, "Twice…" (protected); the long sit, wet to the waist; his bill (Compression in the ribs, Anchor held against biting, the read at its dearest under water). **The exchange** (protected) ending "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-29-- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-30-- **Day 121, the finding:** "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." The kit's bearing is the same line. The fourth circle is three days out. "I'm telling you where I'll be." / "That's a healer's sentence." / "I know whose it is."
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-41-- **No new maker sentence**: only "Someone made this pattern." and "a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-42-- **The instruments read true in Cael's hand.** Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-43-- Lira's order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"). The ankle is unmended. Brom's shoulder is bound, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow is with Lira, with one bolt left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:44:- **Ninety-six in hand. Nine lines. Eleventh.** The kit is on the table. Fifty-two sheets.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-45-- Everything in `BOOK_MAP.md` §1 "Ending" is binding, as Book 8 Ch1 opens on it.
