editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-23-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-24-The deliberate quieter movement. Its reason: integration cost, the midpoint disclosure and the birthday, between the Ring and the Stair. Its action is learning. Cael turns nineteen with the lights on inside himself; the Quieting gets its name; Lira hears it first; and the instrument gets a rule before it is ever turned outward. Turns and promises:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-25-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:26:- **The telling on the table** is explicitly a retelling to Oryn of what Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln already established in edition B6: his own Arbiter woke at Kindling; the station plate lit eleven seconds late; the failed-safe word replaced the old name; the Arbiter then went dark. Sources are named by Path, not by person, except the three Oryn has touched. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4, B7] The notice said aloud. The page fetched from the loft and read twice in its counted places. **Her answer** (protected): "So I couldn't read you because…" … "Then use it on yourself first. Before anyone… I want to be the one you tell." Oryn's new condition governs Tide reading outward: self first, then ask first every time. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4] "You're the colour of the wall…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-27-- **The cascade: it listens, it doesn't pull (three nights).** His own current at the edge of every thought; the nine coming up out of it one at a time and told apart by sound; "a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on." Brom on the ladder ("How many people." / "Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with." / the forge story). Day two: **Storm heard resettling** in the yard, a hand on the well's rim; the ground arriving half a beat late under a counted foot, so he **relearns the Wind economy in the yard** while the listening runs (a learning encounter). **Oryn's "Where is it loudest."** "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer." Ask first, said in the yard: "I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-28-- **Karis documents** in a dry-hinge voice ("For now."; "You have an instrument now. It's not mine… I'm entering that I know that.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-29-- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** arrives by carter: “Six went in. Six came out.” It lands against Cael's memory of Gault's last line, *The instruments will not see its like.* Gault's physical leaf remains in the west with the withdrawal file and is not among the party's papers. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D5, N5] Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-30-- **The first self-reading** that night, alone, as she set it. Ten flows and no banks (a limit of the reading, written above everything else). Then **the place session nine logged**: not a current, not the tenth, not any of the nine; near the middle, where everything is nearer; the ten go *round* it. Three things he can count. It is **not named**: no "still place" yet. The inventory, and **the three words retired with the reason** (protected). "Hundred and two in hand; six to the hold for the room and the kid."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:31:- **The week of tables (days 103–109).** The ring laid flat (eleven sheets cut to the uprights' heights); the tally of *kinds* she will not number from one site. **Five findings, each a scene:** (1) *the Quieting*: grammar for a process, not a place; (2) **identical failure** across five sigils (Iron R1, Copper, no ranking, Bronze, Iron R4; Lira's clock in Lira's words), and the looms sentence, unfiled (protected); Seln's "Six… I'm counting it." and the struck six; (3) **the strata as a physical demonstration** (four chips oldest to the right; the knife marked and the floor didn't; no stroke, no join, no laid edge; weathering past the founding stone), with **[UNBOUND] once** (protected), then Brom's "Say it with less."; (4) **the stakes, once, in four sentences**; (5) **the observation entered and the interpretation stopped**: "It's a fear." / "Does it help?" / "It's just correct." Oryn works the hold in the yard (nine late here, eleven at the next) and looks at the table once.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-32-- **New, a learning arc: Lira and the bowman.** The bowman off the gate-walk (unnamed) teaches her to shoot braced one-armed, against a rail and a knee, with the steading's bow spanned for her because she cannot span one-armed and says so. Short sessions, his few words, her fierce economy. This plants the Hall (M8). Oryn's order is kept exactly: the left arm holds nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-33-- **C2, staged:** Oryn decides to leave her mule with the crew. Three boxes and a girl with one arm need it more than a healer whose holds keep beasts. She will take the next hold's beast at Millrace. Her decision, said in her register.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-34-- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-13->
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-14-> Movement 5 must inherit the following facts not fully carried by its packet:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-15->
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:16:> - **Correct Ring geometry:** western line stone to floor centre is 220 yards as printed; the floor is 26 of Cael's yard-strides across; the den is at the eastern lip. Therefore den to the western objective line is about 233 yards, and den to the eastern perimeter is about 207 yards. Do not reintroduce M4's discarded 150-yard figure (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:43-45,165-169,199-201`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:64-66`). The cord is approximately 21.9 yards by the protected circumference/radius figures, but its length and Karis's stride remain unstated (`manuscript/chapter-28.md:191-209`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-17-> - **Lane:** the trodden cord-lane runs west from the floor through the western stone; the six are on the wrong/eastern side of the floor from it (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:9-29,199-201`). M5's 160-to-60 count must be staged within that longer approximately 233-yard retreat (`MOVEMENT-005.md:24`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:18:> - **Rubbings after fix 7:** eleven complete Ring sheets exist; the last is rolled in Karis's coat and the others are in the middle box (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:99,131-163,237`; `BOOK_MAP.md:35`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-19-> - **Bodies at dusk:** Cael's ribs remain taped until day 99 and his calf remains bound, not mended; Lira's tibia is new and barred from running until about day 110, her ankle remains unmended/taped, and she has drawn her knife; Brom's wrist is sound; Karis is three parts full; Seln is unmarked; Oryn cannot read or mend inside (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:23-43,181-233`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:207-215,237`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:169-179`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-20-> - **Secret/action count:** Cael alone knows the Iron read, foot of Wind and floor read worked. Shadow is unused; deployment since the Line remains one, and the day-96 log deliberately has no deployment line (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:239-299`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:63-77,219-235`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-21-> - **Live Arbiter result:** Karis, Brom, Seln, Lira and Oryn fail at the same step; Cael's Arbiter was already dark and remains described only that way. Oryn knows no fragment mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:189-229`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:181-233,283-297`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-22-> - **Hounds are still sign only:** Seln reads eight or nine fresh outward tracks to the east and none back; M5 may make the packet's nine visible, but no M4 character has yet seen one (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:155-193`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:18,24`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-23-> - **Exact party/object placement:** six at the den; Brom wears the middle box; Seln is on one knee; Oryn's mule is hobbled west of the line stone with two panniers, six borrowed blankets, the unused left boot and covered crossbow; two boxes remain in Thornwater, with the reserve sealed in the third (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:13-29`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:3-7,219-239`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:167,183`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:24:> - **Site evidence:** no instruments were found on the floor or within forty yards; stake 31 is registry-stamped, about five years weathered and untouched; the eleven uprights and lip carry unknown bands; Karis's chips match nothing (`manuscript/chapter-28.md:107-143,219-235`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:53-123`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:25:> - **Maps and withheld memory:** Karis's calfskin has three circles, two marked *guess*; the registry sheet has seven dashed roads and the Fallow is the third. Seln has not yet supplied his map-memory inference; that remains M5's (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:109-149`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:54-56`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:25-26`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:26:> - **Accounts/open obligations:** 108 marks in hand; one sixty-yard four-strand rope owed in kind; the two HOLD slips remain unresolved; the Fallow hundred remains lodged against the broker's mark (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:3-21,227-245`; `manuscript/chapter-25.md:229-253`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:181-185`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-27-> - **Letters:** Ephram, Vell and Hesk remain unanswered in Hesk's satchel; Bracken is male and Vell's session remains unexplained (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:59-83`; `manuscript/chapter-27.md:55-101`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:169,189`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-28-> - **Oryn's route choice:** she replaced four extra table days plus the added deep-reading day with this road, explicitly owing Thornwater's short bench on return; she has been round the Ring by the ruts thirty times but had never crossed (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:223-231`; `manuscript/chapter-26.md:195-215`; `manuscript/chapter-27.md:249-253`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-29-> - **Cael's command error:** he spent a quarter-hour past his declared two-hands limit, entered it against himself, and the sun is half gone (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:125-163,199-205,237-239`). That cost belongs to the M5 opening pressure.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-34-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-35-## Where we enter
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-36-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:37:Dusk on the 96th, at the Ring's far lip, Seln standing up off his knee. The floor goes white. Nine low grey shapes cross the white without a sound.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-38-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-39-## What this movement is for
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-40-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-41-The Quiet as terrain: the book's central set piece, won by the one thing on the floor that can still be loud. Then the night it costs; the camp that does not ask; and the covenant written *before*, which buys the tenth fragment honestly. Turns and promises:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-42-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:43:- **The Ring (≈8,000–9,500 across two chapters), a retreat with a geometry.** The line is the objective. Nine counted on the white. "The road's cut." / "The grass. Where the cord went." Brom holds the lip: a hand's-height drop that robs a hound of drive, the haft, a man the pack cannot hear. Lira runs the rim's turned edge; the ankle goes a third time; the forearm taken and held; she cannot burst it off. **Brom's bolt through the eye at thirteen feet.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] Oryn's hands: "Nothing… Nothing in my hands." Cloth and knees. "Move. I can't fix this here. Move." Brom's string opens his fingers in the dark. The lane counted down, 160 to 60, the scrub moving at Lira's pace and never showing a shape. They are *careless* in here, because no prey has ever shouted. **Karis down at sixty**, hands on a throat, the jaws closing across her fists, the loudest sound on the ring. **Shadow, once, ten strides**. Only Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln have the sightline; Oryn is screened by Brom and fixed on Lira/Karis, sees no discontinuity and cannot attribute the movement. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B2] The throw. Then *he stops holding*: Wind full, north off the lane; every head turns; then everything, one after another, so there is never a breath when he is not the loudest thing on the floor. Pressure for noise; Ember held out; Blade ringing with nothing to cut; Storm seeding the rut, the Iron/body read already released to the air and unavailable under his soles until the lane is relinquished [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B3]; Anchor off its hold and looking west. North to the rut, **east the wrong way** about a hundred and thirty yards, back west. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] Seln's "Back" from the stone and Lira's a breath after. The second lock with Compression at contact. Over the stone. **The bolt at six feet.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] From within ten feet, Anchor's perception sees Karis's points before they light [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1]: **the wall of ignition along the line's inside edge**, from her knees, voiceless. Seven break out north and south along the outside; two dead. Win-sentence and costs on the page. The opponent learned nothing it could use, because it had never needed to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-44-- **The hour's mending at the line by lantern:** "There. Back." (she does not mention the clock). The state, said because a thing not said is not a finding. **The order (protected, exact)** and the sling; "One arm. From here to the snow."; "The ankle's a tape and a season…"; Oryn flat on the road. Karis's written lines. Seln: "Nothing." Brom: "Hand." / "Morning. Wash it. I've nothing tonight." The log, including **the Book 9 plant line, exactly.** Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes." / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:45:- **The camp at the stone (night of the 96th → dawn of the 98th):** the unfiled entry (protected). Morning arithmetic aloud: Karis's throat ("Days. Hoarse before it's anything."); Brom's hand ("String… That's two."); **Cael's calf read and not mended**, the fourth failure ("I don't say a finding four times to a patient and change it on the fifth."). Oryn against the stake: "Three in two days… That's a route." The route's far end, eleven days north. **Seln at the stake**: the charcoal circle from memory lies on the carter's circle; "Ignorance doesn't stamp iron."; "The Compact knows what quiet ground does. And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." (once); "No… I carried the maps. I never saw the file." Karis: *Where*, then *Entered as said*, then *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* **The contract re-read:** a question, not a recovery; "We just told them."; "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six." The dead hound dragged off and the bolt cut out (five in the sleeve); rations in sixths; nobody says *yours*. Second-night log. **Dawn of the 98th: Oryn's eight crossings alone.** He watches and does not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-46-- **Two days back (98–99):** Lira walking flat-footed as she is told; the calf closing with no count on the flat by the second noon. **Thornwater:** "Six. Well." Tape off in the yard ("Twenty-one days. A rib is six weeks. These are done."). The calf closed in four days. "Still and whole." / "You don't get a yes. You get told." / "What does helping look like?" / "I'll know."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-47-- **The loft council, without her:** the conditions as he built them (sustained; stakes on both sides; earnest, on him and not against him); Karis's torn sentence (protected); the price; Lira: "Then tell her. Tonight. Before."; his argument, and its honest underside ("the real one is that I don't know what she'd say"); Seln's "nearest thing to it… I'd enter both."; Brom's "What's it cost her?". **The covenant written before** (protected, whole).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md-48-- **Day 100, the deep reading (≈4,500):** the back room fixed from the door (window, table, stool, the roll in her order); "Breathe like a man asleep."; the count of ten ("Nothing. As before."); then the long one. The current goes *along*, not down; she can be felt keeping time; her commentary on banks (Iron Skin walled, Ember hot, Wind too fast to feel), "there's more water"; Shadow draws in under her touch; Storm quiet; he understands she is not afraid of him, because her trade has no room for being impressed; "Eleven years…". **The conditions arrive.** He could stop it, and stopping would be the lie. *He reached. Directed. Open-eyed. Still.* **The notice, exactly.** Two firsts counted; the third not written. "Something just changed…" / "No. I did. I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it…"
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-20-- **The seal:** Shadow-adjacent is sealed from any witness who could carry the seeing west, because a defector's tradecraft in Cael's hands would confirm the surveillance-era acquisition. It costs from waking and drifts at dusk. Cael leaves it sealed past the Line; deployment since the Line is none. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D1, D3; F-rerun F2.4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-21-- **Companions:** Lira, Wind, Iron R1 retained; Silver evaluation declined at full price. Brom, Iron Skin, Copper formal for good, continental Copper champion; Iron finding unsigned. He left the last Velmere letter sealed and unopened on his table at Halcenvane, with the unsigned finding; he carries no family letter east (edition B6 ch56). Karis, Ember, Iron R3 retained; research standing, budget/allocation, annex, archive privileges and restricted-collection access lapsed; three boxes made into a field archive. Seln, Shadow, Bronze, fifteen years' service; left without notice or form, four keys surrendered; brought the locked case east in his own satchel; it now rides under the canvas. All five have no open injury. Lira and Brom have read the log. Karis sees demonstrations, not the log. Seln has known the mechanism since edition B6 ch37; he recognized that Cael kept his file; his “twice more” allowance remains two. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D2, B5, C2; coordinator O1, O2]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-22-- **Who knows:** the integration mechanism is known to the five travelers and nobody else. The cache/falsification history is known to those five plus Vastin; Vastin does not know the mechanism. Ephram knows only the departure and the deliberately managed band. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit N6]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:23:- **Objects:** a two-wheeled cart; a brown gelding with one white foot; three numbered boxes and Seln's locked case under one canvas; the pooled Book 6 purse; two no-return-address letters, to Hesk and Vell, written at the shelf and held for the first westbound carrier. Daeva's reply already went west from the first water beyond the Line. The registry's printed continental sheet and the Ternhall straightedge are in Karis's middle box. Karis has marked the sheet *ridge* and *Shelf; a pine; water at 36*. Lira's separate route book reads *Ridge: one horse, three boxes by hand. Scree: by hand again. Shelf.* [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D3, D5, N3, N4, N7; coordinator O2 (the case rides under the canvas)]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-24-- **Compact posture:** the file reads *Status: active non-compliance, observation priority escalated.* Asset-restriction is *pending jurisdiction*: it will be served within the hour if any one of the four enrolled names is written in a book inside a district. The last watcher turned back at the provincial marker. The author of the fifth file line is unnamed, and no office is named on it. Vastin remains inside as Archmarshal / the certifying office and returned the closing summary without annotation. Gault remains evaluator of record. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit C3, D5]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-25-- **Quiet ground:** unknown to every one of them. Nobody has heard the words.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-26-- **The last line:** "nothing anywhere was deciding what he was, except him."
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-32-- **The rule on the tenth, in Oryn's hand and his:** *ask first, every time.* It was paid once, by not reading Teague.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-33-- **Lira:** left forearm bitten through at the Ring, mended at the line, reopened on the Stair and closed again. **Still slung and under Oryn's order at first snow** ("She'll say when"). Right ankle taped and **never mended in this book.** Carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap (hers from the Hall, Ch21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-34-- **Brom:** right shoulder bolted on the Stair and mended, reopened in the Hall and mended a second time ("Twice… not three times this season"). Then bound by Teague's healer of no Path and carried guarded. Carries the kit and the middle box.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:35:- **Karis:** holds the field archive: **52 sheets** of copied walls (Ring 11 / Stair 29 / Hall 12); the kit's **field ledger** (given her by Seln on the road home); the carter's map with **four circles and the bearing**; the Ternhall straightedge. She named the Quieting. Her hypothesis stays unentered. She has the inn's back room for the sheets.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-36-- **Seln:** unmarked all book. The case carried, unopened, targeted, kept. Angry once (the Stair's rim: "No faces." and a broken stock).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-37-- **Oryn:** at Thornwater on her route, **three weeks late there** and the route whole. Letter: "Six, by letter." She learned the mechanism on the 100th. She has not heard any theory, because there is none.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-38-- **Who knows the mechanism:** six (Oryn added). Teague, Pike, the holds and the faceless faction do not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:39:- **Pike's board:** **nine completed lines** under the five names (the last three are the traverse, the Ring and the Stair). The Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The **season line** has been read aloud. **No line number entered**: "First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." The five names stay **eleventh** on the wall, unchanged.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-40-- **Teague:** "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew (four plus an older healer of no Path) stays at Lowmarch through the cold term. He has given the axe-head hold's long fence (forty, HOLD) to the five for the cold term. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; restates protected Ch24 — OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-41-- **Money:** **ninety-six in hand** (a hundred and two, less six to the inn for the back room). Three hundred entered as taken and never to be paid.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:42:- **Objects:** the kit (case, pacing cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar mark and a bright point, mallet); the ledger; the 52 sheets; the map; **two brass straightedges** (Ternhall's; Hesk's, arrived on the last ferry). Both touch the three paced centres without daylight, **in Cael's hand as in anyone's** (Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair of error). Also three boxes, Seln's case, one mule (the crew's), and Oryn's crossbow with one bolt left in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-43-- **The Quieting, as known:** four sites on one alignment. The Fallow Ring, the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall have been entered. The fourth was paced from outside on the 123rd: **about four hundred and forty yards' radius** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2], ringed by a **cordon of iron stakes numbered thirty-four, with the stroke-and-bar mark, a pace apart**. Not entered, not named, its effect unknown, its central shape a standing grey thing nobody has a word for. "Someone made this pattern." was said once and not answered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-44-- **The Compact:** knows quiet ground exists and what it does, and which crew walks out of it (a completion report on the Fallow contract; the rim on the Stair saw a practitioner walk out *declaring*). **It does not know that anything works inside.** Asset-restriction is still pending. The nameless second Anchor hand: "the account's getting longer."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-45-- **Letters west on the last ferry:** to Hesk ("Nineteen, past the Line, and there's a roof…") and to Vell ("There's a second ledger on the continent…").
--
