editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-266-- Hesk's note with the straightedge (Ch24): *Nineteen. I'm told it's late; the ferry's fault, not mine. Your grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. This one's true to a hair. Mind the shape. — H.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-267-- Cael to Hesk (Ch24): *Nineteen, past the Line, and there's a roof. It's an inn. The shape you said to mind is a line, and I've got the tool for it now. — C.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-268-- Cael to Vell (Ch24): *Vell. There's a second ledger on the continent with my name in it, kept by a one-armed man in a town on no map, and this week he stopped numbering me. He said his book was wrong about us by being too small. You said once that somebody should have a record that doesn't answer to the Compact. There are two now. The session still stands. — C.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:269:- **Oryn's letter (Ch24):** *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.* — then: Six, by letter. (The architecture and series docs still quote "eleven days"; prose and Book 8 say **three weeks**. See C6.) [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
