editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-298-- Ch1: "You're paper, aren't you" … "Then you know how to keep quiet. Keep it." — Seln: "Don't declare anything." — Lira: "I could clear it." / "No," said Seln. / "I know. I'm saying it so I've said it." — The carter: "First crew I've hired that knew to shut up." — "Stillhound." … "It's a stillhound. You shut up. It went home."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-299-- Ch2: Pike: "Once before it's in, so she can say it's wrong. Once after, so it's said." … "Half this meadow can't read. The book's for me. The saying's for them." — "A Bronze who lost my carter is worth less than a Copper who brought him home. Out here that's arithmetic. In there it was heresy." — Seln: "West of that, the inventory executes the hour any of us shows paper. Pending jurisdiction means armed. Nobody goes west." / Brom: "Nobody wants to." / Karis: "Nobody can. Different sentences." — Pike: "Four lines. Nobody lost, nobody hurt, nobody knows you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-300-- Ch3: "It's because you die," — the steading's woman: "Four," … "Out of five. Two men went down to that ford this month and one came up."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:301:- Ch4: the carter's wife: "You mean the quiet ground? Everybody knows the quiet ground. Nobody goes in." — Lira: "So what am I becoming, exactly, if nobody's measuring?" — Seln: "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report." — Brom: "What does the board pay a man with no Path at all." / Pike: "Same as anyone," … "What'd he do?" — Pike: "Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something. That's not rudeness. That's the ledger."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-302-- Ch5: Seln quoting Pike: "Never be below them. Never be *loud* below them." — Karis: "On a slope, flight is a landslide with legs."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-303-- Ch6: Lira: "That was me," … "The loud thing." — Oryn: "Who's worst?" … "Name's Oryn." … "Tide. Healer." … "Iron. Four, if anybody's keeping a book up here." … "That's one," … "Hands on. That's the only way it works." — "Your ribs are broken," she said. "I can feel that they're broken. I can't feel *you*." … "Whatever you are, I can't read it." … "I've never said that to anyone. Tape them. They'll heal on their own." … "They always have, haven't they?" / "Yes," he said. / "That's not an answer," Oryn said. "That's a *finding*."

