editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-24-- **The bearing walk (116–118), on the page:** a road, then a track, then a carter's memory. Karis does not once say *if*. The country going into the last mild days. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-25-- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and eighty-five yards. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:26:- **The trials (≈2,500), from the hall's outer coping inside the perimeter (EXC-B7-005):** the causeway crossing, with her hands checked at the stride both ways; the rule walking with them; the bulge once in a quarter-hour; a stone at eleven; Lira's skipping stone answered only where it stops, at fourteen; **Seln's rule in his own hand on Karis's page** ("It's blind… it strikes what *stays*."); **Cael's Anchor point** held for sixty counts ("It reads that as the heaviest thing…" / "…the thing that *stays*."). The council at the stone (protected Lira lines). Camp at the line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-27-- **Day 119, the Hall (≈5,000–6,000):** Brom *stops* to put Karis up the wall and the floor opens under him; he puts her up before he goes sideways. "Get *off* the floor." **The coping** as cover and trap. Karis copying the wall she kneels on, funny for exactly one exchange. **Brom's shoulder opens**; he slips on the wrong wall. **Oryn into the water, skipping**, the healer reaching a falling patient (not heroic, only nearest). **The second pass turns** toward where she is going. **Cael in, declaring:** Compression takes the strike into a standing frame at the broken edge; **Anchor laid on the floor** at the broken centre. "A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest." It surfaces whole for the first time in anyone's memory. "Brom. Wall. Your weight. Now." **Four bolts into the pale**: Lira twice, braced one-armed against the coping and a knee, with Seln spanning between (the bowman's lessons pay); Seln twice. The point released; the jaws close on water; it lets go and goes down, alive. "Walls… Twelve sheets." It is left there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-28-- **Costs at the track's end:** Oryn's hour, "Twice…" (protected); the long sit, wet to the waist; his bill (Compression in the ribs, Anchor held against biting, the read at its dearest under water). **The exchange** (protected) ending "Lie still. I want to read you."
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-368-- **Why the job exists (flag):** an Oxhollow cart fetching Thornwater grain goes round by Lowmarch's ferry, eight days each way; the salt crews speak of a shelf over the high ground between, and a mule string once came over it in three days. Oxhollow is "a ford with a fence round it"; its keeper takes a copper a wheel.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-369-- **Which way it is walked (flag):** east to west. The eastern foot is at the lower of the two crossings on the Thornwater road, where a side water comes in from the north; an old cart-track, grown over, climbs it for two hours to a gorge. Thornwater is not visited and the stretch is not walked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:370:- **The smith's terms (flag):** the cart is the party's own, sold on day 12 and cut to a mule's gauge (four feet between the wheels, five from hub to hub). Six marks laid down against its return, which is the hire; six more if it does not come back. Paid at first light on the 71st: in hand, forty-six. It is drawn by hand, two in the shafts.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-371-- **The boxes go (flag):** the ferryman is filling the loft over the drum with hay against the cold and wants all of it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-372-- **Brom's strap:** a doubled bight of the ferryman's long rope over his head and one shoulder, made fast low on the cart's near side; he draws with his chest and keeps both hands behind him. On the bench he walks on the up-slope side and leans against it. **The ferryman's rope went into the gorge with the cart.**
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-380-- **Oryn, as seen (flag):** not tall, square in the shoulder, broad in the hand, hair cropped as short as a boy's; a man's brown coat made for a bigger person and taken in ("off a peg that nobody was using any more", given by a hold in her first year); a low hoarse voice; a small brown mule with a pack-saddle, two panniers and a crossbow in an oiled cover lashed on top. She stops a stride and a half from people. Cael puts her at about ten years older than himself; no age is stated. Her right heel is rubbed raw and taped, and has been for two rounds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-381-- **Tide, as taught (flag):** contact only. What mends is the patient's own current, which stands at a break "like water behind a board"; she finds where it stands, opens the way with her own, and holds it open while the body does six weeks' knitting in under an hour, and she pays for the six weeks. A reserve "like a purse", spent at the rate of what it mends: three mendings in a day if she has slept under a roof and been fed, two on a road. She will not touch a table until she has eaten and slept two hours. She cannot do it to herself. She mends what she can read. **The surface reading:** hands on the hurt, or two fingers on a wrist and two on the neck, for a count of ten; it costs her nothing she would notice. **The deep reading ("the long one"):** both hands, all of her, minutes, the patient still and whole, at a mending's cost; not run on a road. A person's current runs in a bed, and "the shape of the bed is their Path"; she names Karis as Ember by it. **The stall:** a hand on a wrist for a breath as the other means to declare, and the declaration does not come; it costs a day's mendings and the next day's and mends nobody; she has done it and hates it. No count of times is given.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:382:- **Tape (flag):** linen strip three fingers wide, spread with pitch, mutton fat and something from a hold that keeps bees. Five bands from breastbone to spine, laid on the out-breath. Twenty-one days from the 78th; she means to lift it herself. For Lira's ankle: an anchor turn above the joint, two strips under the heel and up the outside, and a figure of eight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-383-- **Brom's wrist:** mended on the 80th; a cuff of plain linen "to remind the hand"; a week from the middle of that day: it takes what sits on it and nothing that hangs from it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-384-- **Oryn's route, as told (flag):** seven holds, twenty days, "thirty-odd" rounds; late eleven times and this the twelfth, five days behind; nobody has put a coin in her hand past the Line; holds feed her and the mule, one shoes the mule, one gave the coat. She began with four holds and added the fifth in her third round, the sixth "for an old woman's sake" and the seventh because of a child. In a city she was one of six on a healing house's staff, where the morning list is kept by tier. No city is named.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-393-**Where everyone is.** The five are at Oxhollow, in the yard and at the ford, with three boxes on the ground against the gate-house wall. Oryn has gone north out of the gate at dusk with her mule, and is due at Thornwater on the 93rd. Teague and his three have crossed the ford southward at dusk with two mules, a day ahead of the five on the Lowmarch road.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-394-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:395:**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst, day 53). Nothing was used on the mountain or since: Anchor, Compression, the Iron read, Wind and Storm all offered and were refused; Shadow sealed. **Three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped with five bands on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break, and Oryn means to lift the tape herself.** Left calf opened along the old bite on the 78th, bound in Oryn's linen, not mended. No log entries for the 78th and 79th. He has been read three times by a healer (the 80th, and twice on the 84th) and has answered three questions truly: his hurts knit in the right places; faster than other people's; no healer has ever got anything from him. He has not asked Oryn south. He has not answered Hesk's letter. Teague has spoken to him and he has said one word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-396-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-397-**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. **One involuntary full burst on the 78th**, when the ledge went; none refused more hardly than the second. **Right tibia broken on the 78th, set and mended on the 80th: straight, new, to walk within the week and not to be run on for a month.** **Right ankle never mended** ("That's a tape and a season. It'll set."); she tapes it herself as Oryn taught her and says that she now knows where it is. Her right boot is under the mountain; she is barefoot on that side. She rode Oryn's mule from the shoulder to Oxhollow and has not said the word. She asked for the ankle once.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-422-- Karis spent nine points/eight channels for eight seconds and is empty; on day 80 Oryn barred even a spark for one week. She could write one line on day 82 and hold the purse on day 84, but that does not release the restriction (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:41-53,279-301`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:215-219,359-361`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-423-- Brom's left wrist is mended under the day-80-to-day-87 rule: it may take what sits on it, nothing hanging from it, and he must release a pulling load. His hedging bill and the older ash wedge survive (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:3-5,267-277`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:37-43`; fix 10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:424:- Cael's three left-low ribs were broken day 78 and received five bands on day 81, to be lifted on day 99 by Oryn if possible; his reopened calf is only cloth-bound. His nine fragments are held, Shadow remains sealed, and deployment since the Line is one (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:121-155`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:3-45`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-333`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-425-- Oryn has failed three surface readings of Cael, knows only that he heals fast with no readable current, knows nothing of fragments, has run no deep reading, keeps no written record, and has put one day on her route for the promised whole-and-still reading (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:317-351`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:53-89,137-155,211-233`). Her mule still carries her panniers and covered crossbow; do not spend owner decision #24 early (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:143-159`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:103-107`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-426-- After fixes 6–9, Teague knows only what his own schedule and the yard/keeper show: he missed Oryn on day 81; on day 84 the five have no cart, have healer-made bindings, delivered a paid no, and all survived. He does not know they caused Oryn's lateness and knows nothing of fragments or the mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:237-295`; fixes 6–9).
