editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-436-### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-437-- **The line (OWNER-pending #49, default in force).** At the line the five live Arbiters stop at the same step: Karis's, Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's. Cael's own Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling and nothing in him changes there; his fragments go on answering inside. The protected log entries are word for word (their loose "mine" is his shorthand). Outside them nothing says "his Path", nothing says his Arbiter is awake or unaffected, and nothing says WHY the fragments answer. The word *Quieting* has not been said. "Compact" has not been said aloud: the stake carries the registry stamp. "Made" has been said of the place once, by Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:438:- **Cael's two private tests** (day 96, a quarter of an hour, a cord north of the stone, unwitnessed) are NOT deployments and are not logged as such. Deployment since the Line stays ONE. Shadow untouched. He has told nobody; his reasons are on the page and he distrusts them. The day-96 log omits the deployment line for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-439-- **Ring geometry — the manuscript governs (Movement 5 inherits):** the western line stone is 220 yards from the floor's middle; the floor is 26 of Cael's yard-strides across; the den is under the floor's EASTERN lip; so den to the western line is about 233 yards and den to the eastern perimeter about 207. The protected round is 1,374 yards and a piece (sixty-two cords and twenty strides); radius ten cords; the constant offset is six and a half feet per cord. NO cord length and NO stride length is stated, and none is to be added. "A hundred and fifty yards inside" is dropped from the plan.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:440:- **Sixty-two cords; stake 31; eleven uprights; eleven Ring sheets, all finished** on the 96th. The registry's stakes ring the place. No stillhound has been SEEN: prints and a den, all sign. The movement ends at dusk at the far lip, about to move.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-441-- **The trials at the line** ran Karis, Brom, Seln, Lira, Oryn. Lira's full burst became one step; her words on stepping back out are the protected clock line. Oryn has crossed twice (with Brom; with the six) and reads nobody inside; her eight solo crossings are Movement 5's. Seln's map memory is Movement 5's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-442-- **Pike spoke of Teague unasked, to the ledger:** Teague read the Fallow slip twice, put it back under the stone and took the fence. Teague has no stated reason. The two HOLD slips are unresolved ("a fortnight, then Teague").
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-503-**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. All six know what quiet ground does to a live Arbiter, to the stride, and that a healer's hands stop there. The party knows that the registry's iron stands on the line, numbered thirty-one, some five years old; that no instruments are at the site; that hounds den under the floor. **Nobody but Cael knows that anything answers inside.** Pike, Teague, the clerk and the holds know only that five people took a paper.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-504-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:505:**Open threads.** Where eight or nine hounds are, at sunset. A lane two hundred yards long and one way out that anybody has walked. A healer who cannot mend east of a stone. A captain's quarter of an hour. What he has not told them, and why. A posting written inside the Line for a thing that is not there. Thirty-one. Two blanks on a calfskin marked *guess*. "A circle is a made shape." A rope, two holds, three unanswered letters, and no roof.
